{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Source Code Repository.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Source Code Repository.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"source code repository source code repository","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Source Code Repository.md","fileName":"Source Code Repository.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Source Code Repository","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:52\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Continuous Integration and Delivery]] [[Git Version Control]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Continuous Integration and Delivery","Git Version Control","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Source Code Repository.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Source Code Repository.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"source code repository source code repository","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Source Code Repository.md","fileName":"Source Code Repository.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Source Code Repository","heading":"Source Code Repository","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A source code repository records versioned application files and provides the revision consumed by the continuous-integration pipeline. A pushed change can serve as the trigger and gives the resulting build an identifiable source state.\n\nThe repository is the pipeline's starting contract: build definitions, application code, tests, and relevant deployment scripts must agree at that revision. Generated artifacts are outputs and should not obscure which source produced them.\n\nIn Git, a repository includes both the working files and local metadata under `.git`, which stores objects, references, configuration, and history. A repository can be initialized in an existing directory or created by cloning another repository.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Continuous Integration and Delivery","Git Version Control","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Source Code Repository.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Source Code Repository.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"source code repository source code repository","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Source Code Repository.md","fileName":"Source Code Repository.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Source Code Repository","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[aspnetcore3andreact.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Continuous Integration and Delivery","Git Version Control","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}